        You will be given the root cause of a bug, the commit message and the corresponding patch.
        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.

        Root cause:
        The bug was caused by the export of iCalendar dates in UTC instead of the local timezone, which led to incorrect date representations, particularly during daylight savings time changes. This issue was introduced in a previous commit (592152d) that defaulted to UTC dates, failing to account for local timezone adjustments.

        Commit message:
        iCalendar Exports

- ensure that the exported dates are in the local timezone
- this fixes the issue with daylight savings that was introduced in commit 592152d
  (Biweekly 0.4.3 defaults to UTC dates)  

